            <ArticleTitle>[Shoulder radiography: useful radiographic views in current practice].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>620-33; quiz 631-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The purposes of this paper are: 1) to review the different radiographic projections commonly used to explore shoulder pathology; 2) to propose a practical approach for radiographic evaluation of the shoulder, adapted to the main clinical situations; 3) to recognize the different imaging features of the most frequent shoulder diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
